    "conclusion": "The depth growth is ~52 stalls/step of ~130-190 us (one per layer-section boundary) plus a slightly larger small-gap floor (4.17 -> 5.15 ms/step). Stalls sit at sub-chain transitions (attention/GR/norm -> MoE burst, MoE -> dense): exposed Python section preparation that appears once the host falls behind far enough for the launch queue to drain at each boundary. Intra-section host reductions are invisible (the build-identity A/B tie), which is why only boundary-exposed work moved the wall at depth. Fix ladder: pipelined next-layer planning during device execution, whole-step HIP graph capture (removes boundary prep and per-launch cost from the steady path), or launch-count reduction by fusion."
